Hundreds of thousands are without power in Florida and Alabama after Hurricane Isayez. This is Omni View North America, episode 17. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. The BBC says the storm was downgraded once it came ashore in Florida. It is still tracking across the southeastern United States. The outage is the change those households are living with while it moves. Colleges across the region in British Columbia are still cutting courses after Ottawa tightened international enrollment in early 2024.

